# 10. AI PLANT DISEASE DETECTION

Build the disease analysis pipeline.

The platform must support an external machine-learning inference service.

Architecture:

Frontend → Supabase Edge Function → ML inference service → Structured results → Database → Dashboard and map.

### Required detection categories

Support configurable disease classes for different crops.

Examples:

- Wheat leaf rust.
- Wheat powdery mildew.
- Wheat septoria.
- Corn leaf blight.
- Rice blast.
- Potato late blight.
- Cotton leaf disease.

Also support:
- Nutrient deficiency.
- Water stress.
- Heat stress.
- Possible pest damage.
- Unknown or unclassified condition.

Do not assume that every crop supports every disease class.

### Analysis results

Each analysis should contain:

- Crop type.
- Detected condition.
- Disease category.
- Confidence score.
- Severity level.
- Affected area, if measured.
- Detection coordinates, if available.
- Image reference.
- Model name.
- Model version.
- Processing timestamp.

### Confidence handling

Use transparent confidence levels.

- High confidence.
- Medium confidence.
- Low confidence.
- Inconclusive.

Do not describe low-confidence predictions as confirmed diagnoses.

If confidence is insufficient, recommend additional inspection or professional agronomist review.

### Critical requirement

Do not create a fake machine-learning model.

If no trained model is connected, the application must show:

"ML inference service is not configured. Disease detection is currently unavailable."

Create a clean inference-service interface so a real trained model can be connected later without rewriting the entire frontend.

Do not claim 89%, 93%, or 95% accuracy unless verified through actual evaluation on a documented dataset.

